(4113, 296, 'proposal', '125 KHZ Proximity Card', '<strong>Customer Additional Expenses:</strong> <br>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Additional Customer Expenses can be of 4 types. Fuel, Inhouse Captain, BBQ and Charges for Boat Maintenance</li>\r\n<li> Customer can Deposit Money through Crtedit Card or Manually (BY Cash, Check or Bank Transfer) </li>\r\n<li>Credit Card Integration</li>\r\n<li>Every time, Customer Uses any of above services, OPerations Team will add these expenses. Which will be automatically Deducted from Customer Account. </li>\r\n<li>Elite Admin can have 3 types of Controls:    </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1. Allow user to have Negative Balance    </li>\r\n<li>2. Dis-Allow user booking in case, his deposit money is not enough.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>- In case Customer is not allowed booking for not having enough balance in Booking, he will not be allowed to book, unless he deposit money.</li>\r\n<li>- Customer can see his Ledger Report</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<strong>Operation Manager:</strong> - Operation Manager will see all daily bookings on his Tablet. - He will update all bookings, in cas ethey are actually used or no show/attendance - After completion of Trip, he will update the system for fuesl used, inhouse Captain or BBQ. He will also update Boat Condition. - Customer will sign the Trip COmpletion Report. <br><br><strong>Administration:</strong> - In case there is a Demage reported in \"Trip Completion Report\", admin will add invoice to customer. Which will be deducted from his deposited cash. - Admin can see all reports, including Deposits/Cash Accounting.', 1.00, 2.00, '', 1, '0000-00-00', '0000-00-00', '0', 0, NULL, NULL, 0, '', 0, 'Y', '0', '0', '0', '0', 'other', ''),
