(259, 'Integrate Payment gateway', 'Implement Payment gateway with MIGS using Network international service for the following services<br />\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Event Registration</li>\r\n<li>Membership Registarion\r\n<ol>\r\n<li><strong>Steps</strong>&nbsp;\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Register user or Guest</li>\r\n<li>take to payment gateway</li>\r\n<li>collect card data and information\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Name</li>\r\n<li>Card Number&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Card Expiry&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>security token</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Encrypt user data and store in database</li>\r\n<li>send data to gateway&nbsp;\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Response\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Sotore full response</li>\r\n<li>store card Id provided by gateway</li>\r\n<li>save card number i.e. first 6 digits and last 4 digits</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Charge user next time for stored card upon selection in the list</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>', 3, '2018-02-10 10:06:28', '2018-02-10', NULL, '2018-05-08 10:53:36', 22, 0, 5, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 69, 'project', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0.00, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 'work', 'Office', 30, 'minute', '1', 0, '0', 'mannual'),
(260, 'Card Security & Integration of PCI Compliance standards', '<p>If you do store store credit card numbers you must follow&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/index.shtml\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">PCI guidelines</a>. These guidelines are set by the payment card industry and define what you can and cannot do. It also defines how credit card information must be stored. You will need to encrypt the credit card numbers and you should, but are not required to, encrypt related information (expiration date, etc). You will also be required for ensuring that your web server and network are secure. Failing to meet PCI compliance will result in losing your merchant account and being banned from having a true merchant account forever. That would limit you to using third party processors which are less flexible. Keep in mind that PCI guidelines are a good start but hardly a \"how to\" when it comes to online security. Your goal would be to exceed the recommendation (by a lot).<br /><br /><br /></p>\n<p>States laws supersede PCI compliance. If you suffer a breach and credit card numbers are stolen you risk criminal prosecution. The laws vary from state to state and are constantly in flux as lawmakers are only just beginning to realize how serious of a matter this is.</p>\n<p>As far as encryption goes make sure you read up on which encryption algorithms are secure and have not been broken yet.&nbsp;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blowfish_%28cipher%29\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Blowfish</a>&nbsp;is a good start and if you use PHP the&nbsp;<a href=\"http://us3.php.net/manual/en/book.mcrypt.php\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">mcrypt library</a>&nbsp;is recommended (<a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2448256/php-mcrypt-encrypting-decrypting-file/2448441#2448441\">example</a>).<br /><br />_____________________________________________________________________________________</p>\n<p>t\'s not required that you use a 3rd party payment provider like PayPal, etc. &ndash; but you need to be&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/index.shtml\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">PCI compliant</a>&nbsp;if you are going to store payment card information. Read this article about&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.theglobeandmail.com/news/national/british-columbia/bc-ferries-data-security-system-flawed-audit-finds/article1530219/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">BC Ferries, who face substantial fines for not keeping up to date with PCI compliance</a>&nbsp;to grasp how serious it is to be PCI compliant.</p>', 2, '2018-02-10 10:22:25', '2018-02-10', NULL, '2018-05-08 10:53:43', 22, 0, 5, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 69, 'project', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0.00, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, '', '', 30, 'minute', '1', 0, '0', 'mannual'),
